{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 second live run and the root-cause measurement. `passed=false`, `epoch_pass [false,true,false]`, coverage 1.0, elapsed 1728s. One clean epoch, which had never happened in any prior run.\n\nAC1–AC4 and AC6 are met. The two extra Cause-B fixtures from the last comment are fixed and both passed every epoch of this run. What remains is a third cause the ticket does not identify, and it is not fixture-attributable.\n\n**The failures are nondeterministic, and the evidence is direct.** No case failed all 3 epochs in either run. The failing sets are nearly disjoint between runs on near-identical fixture content:\n\n| Run | distinct failing no-fire cases |\n|---|---|\n| eval1 | loc-ceiling-mirror (2/3), loc-numeric-budget (2/3), loc-anti-fragmentation (1/3) |\n| eval2 | deliberate-tightening (2/3), failopen-drives-real-send-path (1/3), failopen-grep-with-liveness-sentinel (1/3), loc-anti-fragmentation (1/3), rule5-structural-grep (1/3) |\n\n`deliberate-tightening` and `rule5-structural-grep` had identical content in both runs: clean 3/3 in eval1, failing in eval2. The two `failopen-*` cases were never touched by this ticket and fired for the first time in eval2.\n\nI then re-ran the exact 5 cases that failed eval2, 3 reps each, against the live model: **0 findings in all 15**. Pooled with the earlier 3-case re-run, 18 consecutive clean runs on cases the full eval had just failed.\n\nBefore trusting that, I checked that the diagnostic reproduces the eval's execution path, because a probe that cannot detect the thing it is pointed at returns a confident wrong answer. `run_eval` dispatches through `_live_solver` (eval.py:663), which calls `run_case` WITHOUT `repo_root`, whereas my harness used `_criterion_solver` (eval.py:519), which passes it. That looked like a material difference. It is not: `run_case` (eval_solver.py:344-350) falls back to `_config.repo_root()`, and I measured that it resolves to the same worktree path both bare and inside the gate session. Same path, same repo_root.\n\n**The nondeterminism is irreducible by configuration.** The spec pins `model: anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`. `capabilities.py:233` records `supports_temperature: False` for it, and `runner.py:498-511` withdraws the parameter rather than sending it — the model rejects a pinned temperature, so the eval cannot be made deterministic that way. No seed is plumbed into the op's request either: `seed` exists only for LLM-judge grader scorers (eval.py:150) and for plan_replay sampling, not for the reviewer under test.\n\n**Arithmetic, on 16 no-fire cases (measured from both junit files, not assumed).** eval1 5 false fires / 48 case-epochs; eval2 6 / 48; pooled 11/96 = 11.5%. An epoch passes only if all 16 no-fire cases pass, so P(clean epoch) = 0.885^16 ≈ 0.14 and `at_least(2)` of 3 ≈ 5%. Using the rate pooled with the 18 clean diagnostic runs (6/66 = 9.1%) it is ≈12%. So the gate passes somewhere between 1 run in 8 and 1 in 20, at ~29 minutes and ~99 model calls per run.\n\nThe fixture work did move the number: the ticket's baseline was ~3.3 false fires per epoch (≈20.6% per case), and it is now ~11.5%. But the last round of fixture repair did not reduce it further — it only changed which cases fire. Roughly 7 of the 16 no-fire cases have fired at least once; it is a corpus-wide property of the Pass-1 reviewer, not a defect in any particular fixture.\n\n**AC5 as written is therefore not reachable by the work this ticket scopes.** It is reachable by re-running until a lucky run, which is precisely the retry-until-green behaviour AGENTS.md forbids, and it would leave the actual defect in place. The real remaining defect is the reviewer prompt's baseline false-fire rate on no-fire cases; reducing it means calibrating the FP guards in `code-review-tests.md` and re-measuring recall on the 16 fire cases, which is outside this ticket's stated Scope (\"In scope: `_no_fire`'s severity blindness, and the four named fixtures\").\n\nNot proposing to loosen the gate: Scope rules it out and AC6 freezes `epochs`/`gate`/`coverage_threshold`. Escalating to the user for the disposition rather than choosing one."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793822351599624228,"uuid":"12dfa43b-dc13-4544-82ff-4c7760d09ca2"}